# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  WHY THIS FILE IS AT THE REPO ROOT AND NOT IN ealch-v2/
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# The Expo project is `ealch-v2/`, but the git root is this directory, and EAS
# archives from the GIT ROOT. So `ealch-v2/.easignore` has its patterns resolved
# against THIS directory, one level above where they were written.
#
# That silently broke the anchored ones. `ealch-v2/.easignore` says:
#
#     /android
#     /ios
#
# A leading slash anchors a pattern to the archive root, so those mean
# `Ealchapp/android` and `Ealchapp/ios` — neither of which exists. The real
# `ealch-v2/android` was never matched and uploaded whole: 1,566 MB, roughly
# 87% of a 1.8 GB archive, on the build of 2026-08-20.
#
# The unanchored patterns in that file (`node_modules/`, `.expo/`) DID keep
# working, because a pattern with no leading slash matches at any depth. Which
# is why the archive was 1.8 GB rather than several times that, and why the
# breakage was easy to miss: the file looked like it was working.
#
# Its own header records "the first preview build shipped 214 MB without this
# file" — true at the time, because the native folders had not been generated
# yet. A local `gradlew assembleRelease` created them, and the next cloud build
# carried all of it.
#
# So: patterns here are deliberately UNANCHORED unless they genuinely mean
# "only at the repo root".

# ─── Dependencies. EAS reinstalls from the lockfile. ───────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── Native folders. EAS prebuilds these on the server from app.json. ──────
# Unanchored on purpose: these live at ealch-v2/android, not at the root.
android/
ios/

# ─── The admin workspace. Not part of the mobile build at all. ─────────────
# A Next.js app with its own node_modules, its content scripts, and the
# authoring data. The phone build needs none of it.
ealch-admin/

# ─── Expo / build caches and outputs ───────────────────────────────────────
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── Git history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/

# ─── Seed backups. The bundle needs seed.json and only seed.json. ──────────
# The citation refactor left two 15 MB copies beside it, both untracked:
# seed.post-unit-label.migrated.json and seed.pre-unit-label.14698453.bak.
# They are half the remaining upload and nothing imports them. Patterns rather
# than names, so the next one is caught too.
seed.*.json
!seed.json
*.bak

# ─── Local noise, scratch files and audit output ───────────────────────────
# Measured with _a235_archivesize.mjs: .playwright-mcp alone was 2.3 MB of
# screenshots and page dumps, and the loose _*.txt files another 0.3 MB. Small
# against 29 MB, but none of it is a build input.
*.log
.DS_Store
AUDIT-EVIDENCE/
a1-device/
docs/
.playwright-mcp/
_*.txt
*.apk
*.keystore

# Markdown docs never belong in a build upload (README/AGENTS/CLAUDE/etc.)
*.md
